$ Example PARROT experiment file (synthetic values for testing the converter)
$ Liquidus / solidus tie-lines, Cr-Ni
CREATE_NEW_EQUILIBRIUM 1,1
CHANGE_STATUS PHASE LIQ,FCC=FIX 1
SET_CONDITION P=101325 T=1650
EXPERIMENT X(LIQ,CR)=0.35:0.01, X(FCC,CR)=0.33:0.01
LABEL ATIE
$ table of liquidus points (overall composition given, liquid at amount 1)
TABLE_HEAD 10
CREATE_NEW_EQUILIBRIUM @@,1
CH-ST PH LIQ=FIX 1
CH-ST PH BCC=FIX 0
S-C P=1E5 X(CR)=@2
EXPERIMENT T=@1:5
LABEL ALIQ
TABLE_VALUES
$ T     X(CR)
1700  0.60
1800  0.70
1900  0.80
TABLE_END
$ A thermochemical point - not ZPF, should be skipped
CREATE_NEW_EQUILIBRIUM 20,1
CHANGE_STATUS PHASE LIQ=FIX 1
SET_CONDITION T=1873 P=1E5 X(CR)=0.5
EXPERIMENT ACR(CR)=0.4:0.05
LABEL AACR
